(LEGAL-009 - OPERATIVE CLAUSES & STATUTORY DIRECTIVES \(PAGE 2\)) Tj T*
(Title: L. Krishnan v. State of Tamil Nadu \(2005 \(4\) CTC 1\)  Mandatory Restoration) Tj T*
(Addressed / Competent Officer: District Collector, Revenue Divisional Officer & Executive Engineer \(WRD\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CLAUSE 1: Para 14 \(Absolute Bar on Regularisation of Water-Body Encroachments\)) Tj T*
(The Division Bench held that under Article 21 and Article 48-A of the) Tj T*
(Constitution, the State is a public trustee of all natural water bodies \(eris,) Tj T*
(odais, kulams\) and shall never regularise or grant patta over land classified as a) Tj T*
(water body in the historical revenue records, even if the tank has fallen into) Tj T*
(disuse.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CLAUSE 2: Para 15 \(Direction to Restore Historical Survey Boundaries\)) Tj T*
(District Collectors across Tamil Nadu are directed to identify all encroachments) Tj T*
(in irrigation tanks using original village FMB / A-Register surveys and restore) Tj T*
(the water bodies to their full historical water-spread extent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
